    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0391" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p2/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/P–NSC files, lot 61 D 167, “Indochina”</note>
                <head>No. 251<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State and
                        the Acting Secretary of Defense (Anderson)
                        to the Executive Secretary of the National Security Council (Lay)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-08-27">August 27, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Indonesia</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>References:</head>
                    <item>1. NSC 124/2, “United States Objectives
                        and Courses of Action With Respect to Southeast Asia”.<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d251-f1"/></item>
                    <pb facs="0392" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>
                    <item>2. First Progress Report on NSC 124/2,
                        dated August 5, 1953.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d251-f2"/></item>
                    <item>3. NSC Action 872–b, dated August 6,
                            1953.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d251-f3"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with your request pursuant to Reference (3), there is transmitted
                    herewith a Current Supplement to the Indonesia Section of Reference (2). It is
                    requested that this be circulated to the Members of the Council for their
                    information.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert B. Anderson</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Foster Dulles</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d251-a1.xml" xpointer="d251-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d251-f1" n="1" xml:id="d251-f1-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1952-54v12p1#pg_125">Part 1, p. 125</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d251-f2" n="2" xml:id="d251-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. (S/S–NSC files, lot 63 D 351)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d251-f3" n="3" xml:id="d251-f3-content">
                <p>In this NSC Action, the National Security Council
                    directed its Planning Board to study and make recommendations on the
                    developments in Indonesia. (PPS files, lot 64 D
                    563, box 730)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
